sentences.l:
and from beneath them rose dust
from the plain, which raised the loud-crashing feet of horses,
cutting down with bronze;

and many strong-necked horses
rattled empty chariots along the bridges of war,
longing for their blameless charioteers;

And they past the tomb of old Ilus, Dardanus’ descendant,
through the middle of the plain, past the wild fig tree, were rushing,
eager for the city;

then indeed the father of men and of gods
on the peaks of Ida, many-springed, sat down,
having come down from heaven;
